# Saved coordinates for the native sextet construction

The 1771 proposed sextets are sorted lists of six tetrad masks. The forward
index maps use the literal native generators, and the 252-column matrix
records the proposed covectors. A selected square submatrix and inverse are
included for the injection certificate. These definitions assert no geometric
or linear identities; those require separate kernel proofs.

Source: `../source/README.md`, James, J. Algebra 27 (1973), 57–111,
and the degree-252 ATLAS candidate files. Generated by `source/generate.py`.
-/

